<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	First-party privacy manifest for the JeniFit (plankAI) app target.
	Scope: the APP's own required-reason API usage. Bundled SDKs
	(PostHog, RevenueCat, Lottie, swift-crypto, supabase-swift) ship
	their own PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy covering their usage.

	Required-reason APIs used by first-party code:
	  - UserDefaults (@AppStorage + UserDefaults.standard across 74
	    files): stores this user's own app preferences and app state
	    (onboarding answers, cohort flags, unit choice, per-day notes),
	    readable only within the app/its container. Reason CA92.1 —
	    "Access info from same app, per Apple's documentation." Not
	    tracking, not shared with third parties.

	Re-audited 2026-08-08. Required-reason usage remains UserDefaults
	CA92.1 only — the one systemUptime (system-boot-time) use in
	PlankFood is being replaced with Date in this same release, so no
	boot-time declaration is added. No first-party use of
	file-timestamp, disk-space, or active-keyboard required-reason
	APIs.

	NSPrivacyTracking is true: the app performs ad-attribution
	tracking via the TikTok Business SDK (IDFA access gated by the
	ATT prompt). NSPrivacyTrackingDomains lists the TikTok domains
	that attribution traffic rides; they must stay matched to the ASC
	nutrition label (see 32_PRIVACY_MANIFEST.md).
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array>
		<string>analytics.tiktok.com</string>
		<string>business-api.tiktok.com</string>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
